d=json.loads(P.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def extra(name,level,kind,field,activation,cost,target,duration,frequency,effect,inverted=False):
 ref='SACRED_OATHS[9].'+field
 if any(c.get('sourceRef')==ref for c in d['extraCards']):return
 path=('Oathbreaker — ' if inverted else '')+'Oath of the Martyr King'
 d['extraCards'].append(dict(name=name,level=level,band='Arch' if level<10 else 'Hero',path=path,kind=kind,sourceRef=ref,activation=activation,cost=cost,rangeAndTarget=target,duration=duration,frequency=frequency,effect=effect,prerequisite=f'Paladin {level}; {path}',author='Codex completion of interrupted notebook response'))
extra('Noble Bearing',3,'oathSpell','revelationSpells[0]','Action','2 RP','Up to three allies in your aura','Concentration; three rounds','While RP remains','Selected allies gain +1 on morale checks and saves against Frightened. Once on each of your turns after a paid Smite deals radiant damage, one selected ally gains temporary HP equal to half the actual Smite damage, rounded down, capped at S+M. This replaces, rather than stacks with, the identical King’s Smite temporary HP. Temporary HP never stack.')
extra('Royal Decree',5,'oathSpell','revelationSpells[1]','Action','3 RP','One hearing creature within 30 feet; three selected aura allies','Until end of target’s next turn','While RP remains','Target makes a Wisdom save. On failure it chooses to kneel Prone or move toward you by the safest route using up to its normal Speed on its next turn. It retains its Action and chooses its targets. No self-harm or hazardous route is required. Three chosen allies in your aura gain +1 on morale checks and saves against Frightened until the end of your next turn.')
extra('Burden Shared',9,'oathSpell','revelationSpells[2]','Reaction when an ally takes damage','5 RP','Triggering ally and up to two other willing allies in your aura','One damage event','While RP remains','After applying the original target’s defenses once, divide up to Paladin level+M of the remaining damage among the willing recipients as you choose; each recipient must explicitly accept its amount. The original ally takes the remainder. Transferred damage keeps its type and cannot be reduced again, redirected, reflected or trigger healing/resources. This uses the one redirection event per round.')
extra('Throne’s Grace',13,'oathSpell','revelationSpells[3]','Action','7 RP','Self and up to three allies in your aura','Concentration; three rounds','While RP remains','Your Lay on Hands and touch-range Paladin healing can target selected allies anywhere in your current aura with clear line of effect. Normal activation, pool/RP costs, rank gates and use limits remain. Rolled healing you grant them adds 1 HP per die, maximum S+M additional HP per effect; pool-point healing adds no dice bonus. Selected allies gain +1 on death saves. The spell itself restores no HP.')
extra('Last King’s Gift',17,'oathSpell','revelationSpells[4]','Reaction before ally falls to 0 HP','10 RP','One living ally in your aura','Instant prevention; temporary HP until lost or encounter end','Once per encounter per ally','When damage would reduce the ally to 0 HP without killing it outright, it instead remains at 1 HP and gains temporary HP equal to your Paladin level after the triggering damage resolves. This does not reverse a completed death, remove Wounds or replenish any resource.')
extra('Crown Undying',20,'finalOathGift','finalOathGift','Bonus Action','0 RP','Up to three selected allies in your aura','Three rounds; no concentration','1/long rest','For three rounds apply Crown of Embers protection without consuming its short-rest use. Selected allies reduce their first damage each round by S and gain +1 on saves; this save bonus does not stack with Aura of the Crown. You may redirect from up to two selected allies each round, at most Paladin level+M damage total per round, without a Reaction. Original-target defenses apply once; redirected damage cannot be reduced again. Each protected ally then heals half the damage you actually absorbed for it, rounded down, maximum S+M per ally per round. This is a finite Final healing exception, cannot heal you, cannot exceed maximum HP, and cannot trigger another redirection or heal-copy chain. It does not reset the daily Lay on Hands pool.')
extra('Death Touch — Usurper’s Grasp',3,'deathTouch','oathbreaker.deathTouch','Action','Declare and spend 1 through 2S+M current Lay on Hands points, even on miss','One creature in melee reach','Damage immediate; stolen benefit until end of your next turn','While current pool remains; one theft at a time','Make a divine melee attack using PB+CHA. On hit deal necrotic damage equal to points spent. The target makes a Charisma save. On failure suppress one temporary numerical AC, attack or save bonus of +1 or +2 from a non-innate buff on it; you gain the same bonus, capped at +1. If no eligible buff exists, there is no theft. Never steal permanent passives, class engines, proficiencies, resources, resistance, immunity, actions or another theft. A new theft ends the previous one.',True)
extra('Crownshatter Decree Aura',3,'oathbreakerAura','oathbreaker.aura','Passive','0','Up to three selected enemies in your aura','While conscious and in aura','Each incoming healing event','A selected enemy receives HP healing only if it has taken actual damage from a meaningful hostile creature since the start of its previous regular turn. If it has not, that healing restores 0 HP; its source still spends its normal costs. Temporary HP, stabilization and resurrection are not HP healing for this restriction. This aura never creates damage, transfers healing or reverses recovery that already resolved.',True)
extra('Crownshatter Decree',11,'blasphemousWord','oathbreaker.blasphemousWord','Action','2 RP','One willing ally in your aura','Until end of your next regular turn','1/short rest; replaces shared Signature use','With the ally’s agreement, transfer one temporary +1 or +2 numerical AC, attack or save bonus from a non-innate effect on that ally to yourself, capped at +2. The ally loses that bonus during the transfer. Its source duration/concentration continues and expiration ends your stolen bonus. Never copy a permanent passive, class engine, action, resource, spell use, resistance, immunity or another theft. This does not extend or recharge the original effect.',True)

def card(name):return next(c for c in d['extraCards'] if c['name']==name)
def add(s):
 if s not in d['engine']:d['engine'].append(s)
add('Oath integration limits: one paid Smite total per round, including the level-7 Reaction; one Oath-aura reactive event per round. Multiple damage-redirection options share one event per round unless Crown Undying expressly allows two. Apply original-target defenses once, then split actual damage; transferred damage cannot be mitigated again, reflected, redirected again or generate resources. This explicit rule supersedes wording that permits recipient defenses again.')
add('Sustained Oath spell damage/healing zones use concentration, at most three pulses, and 1 RP upkeep after the first pulse unless a priced card expressly supplies a different finite cadence. Native Oath auras retain their printed passive cadence and target cap. Final auras last their stated finite duration and include their pulses. All hard-denial effects, including compelled Actions, share the common once/source/target/encounter guard; later failures only remove Reactions and reduce Speed by half for one turn.')
add('An emergency Reaction whose trigger itself incapacitates you, such as Grace Reversal or Thorn Crown, may resolve before that incapacitation only if you had a Reaction available before the triggering event. This grants no other actions while incapacitated. Narrative labels such as oppressor require a specific act of captivity/coercion established in the scene, not an alignment or identity assumption.')
add('The source ceiling’s half-pool-per-round Lay on Hands cap is a preserved alternative. This pilot instead uses maximum class level per ordinary Lay on Hands Action and the explicitly once-per-long-rest level-17 Wave that distributes the current remaining pool. No normal heal gains the Wave’s exception.')
c=card('Final Verdict');c['effect']='The marked target makes a Constitution save, taking 4S d8 radiant damage on failure or half on success. On failure it also cannot regain HP until the end of its next turn. If that damage reduces it to 0 HP, use ordinary Downed/death rules; there is no percentage-HP execution. On success your next Smite against it before the end of your next turn uses maximum damage dice. This bounded damage replaces the source draft’s automatic reduction to 0 HP.'
c=card('Verdict Absolute');c['effect']=c['effect'].replace('creatures of your choice in your aura','up to three hostile creatures in your aura');c['effect']+=' The Lay on Hands refill requires a meaningful nonsummoned hostile defeated in a real encounter; staged or willing sacrifices do not qualify.'
